<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhaskaravarman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 600–650</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhaskaravarman was the greatest king of the Varman dynasty of Kamarupa in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, ruling in the first half of the 7th century. He allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shashanka">Shashanka</a> of Gauda and, after Shashanka's death, took his capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnasuvarna">Karnasuvarna</a>. He received the Chinese pilgrim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanzang">Xuanzang</a> around 643, and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate grants are key sources for early Assam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhaskaravarman.jpg" alt="Bhaskaravarman" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chaipau · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kamarupa_Kingdom_of_Bhaskar_Varman.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
